1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,690
You have about seventy lakh rupees in

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,510
India, and a hundred and twenty thousand

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:06,390
dollar job offer in Vancouver,

4
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,510
with the visa and the move paid

5
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:09,250
for.

6
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:10,890
But the day you land,

7
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:13,370
Canada sees you in two strange ways.

8
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:15,910
To the tax office,

9
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:18,030
you just bought everything you own,

10
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,350
at that day's price.

11
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:21,970
And to a landlord or a bank,

12
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,970
you have no history at all.

13
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,210
Not a single day.

14
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:27,870
This guide fixes both,

15
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:28,870
step by step.

16
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,740
The trip itself:

17
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:34,040
Bangalore or Mumbai to Vancouver.

18
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,220
The shortest path arcs north,

19
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:38,540
over Siberia and the edge of the

20
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:41,480
Arctic, about twelve and a half thousand

21
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,280
kilometres.

22
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,840
Most flights connect on the way.

23
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:46,480
Five parts:

24
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,540
before you fly,

25
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,060
your first weeks in Vancouver,

26
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,400
your money back in India,

27
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,680
tax and investing in Canada,

28
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:54,560
and life at work.

29
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,100
First, what you're moving.

30
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,620
Mutual funds are the biggest piece,

31
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,240
about twenty seven lakh.

32
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:03,660
Then gold, bank savings,

33
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,400
provident fund, and the rest.

34
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,620
That's about seventy point four lakh rupees.

35
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,300
At about sixty eight and a half

36
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:12,840
rupees to the dollar,

37
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:14,680
it's roughly a hundred and two thousand

38
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:15,980
Canadian dollars.

39
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,880
So don't move it all at once.

40
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,000
Part one:

41
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:21,380
before you fly.

42
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,360
Start about two months out.

43
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:25,460
Step one:

44
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:28,320
open a Canadian bank account from India.

45
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:31,300
RBC and Scotiabank both take applicants from

46
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:34,400
India online, and RBC's takes about fifteen

47
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:34,960
minutes.

48
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,760
You can wire money in before you

49
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:38,480
land:

50
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:40,460
up to seventy five thousand dollars at

51
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,020
RBC.

52
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,300
Then you activate the account at a

53
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,460
branch when you arrive.

54
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:47,080
How much should you send while you're

55
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,080
still resident?

56
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,413
India lets you send up to two

57
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:52,780
hundred and fifty thousand US dollars a

58
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:53,640
year.

59
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:54,980
But above ten lakh,

60
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,560
banks collect twenty percent tax at source.

61
00:01:58,520 --> 00:01:59,880
Send fifteen lakh,

62
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,200
and one lakh is held back as

63
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,140
TCS.

64
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:04,880
It isn't lost:

65
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,260
you claim it back in your Indian

66
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,400
tax return.

67
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:09,100
But it's locked up for months.

68
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,960
So before you fly,

69
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:13,380
send up to ten lakh,

70
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,620
about fourteen and a half thousand dollars,

71
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,920
for your first three months.

72
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,820
Once you're an NRI,

73
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,000
send more from an NRO account,

74
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,580
up to a million US dollars a

75
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,240
year, with no TCS.

76
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:26,600
And compare exchange rates,

77
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:27,400
not just fees.

78
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,960
Next, health cover.

79
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:31,900
B.C.'s medical plan,

80
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,920
MSP, has a wait:

81
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,280
the rest of the month you arrive,

82
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,240
plus two more months.

83
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,660
Land on March tenth,

84
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,350
and you're covered from June first.

85
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:43,260
So for those months,

86
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,120
buy private health insurance before you leave,

87
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,680
unless your employer's plan covers the MSP

88
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:49,640
wait.

89
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:52,340
Big employers start benefits on day one,

90
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:55,500
but extended health usually tops up MSP

91
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,340
rather than replacing it.

92
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,040
Ask HR.

93
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,660
Pack your paper trail:

94
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,540
passport and permit letter,

95
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:05,380
job offer, degrees and transcripts,

96
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:08,560
experience letters, your driving licence and record,

97
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,080
and medical records.

98
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,760
Two small things.

99
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,060
Keep your Indian SIM active for bank

100
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,920
passwords, and save your statements on landing

101
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:18,700
day.

102
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,480
You'll see why.

103
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,820
Part two.

104
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,460
Your first weeks in Vancouver.

105
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,520
It starts at the airport.

106
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,660
At the border,

107
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,980
an officer issues your work permit.

108
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,180
Check your name,

109
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,820
employer and dates before you walk away.

110
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,140
Carrying ten thousand dollars or more in

111
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:36,880
cash?

112
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:37,600
Declare it.

113
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,800
Day one:

114
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,360
your Social Insurance Number,

115
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:44,800
online or in person with Service Canada.

116
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,400
It's free.

117
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,100
On a work permit,

118
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:49,460
it starts with a nine and expires

119
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,300
with your permit.

120
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,420
At the branch,

121
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,800
activate your account,

122
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:55,080
get your debit card,

123
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,480
and ask for a newcomer credit card.

124
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,280
The big banks approve these with no

125
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,620
Canadian credit history.

126
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,760
The same week,

127
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:05,740
apply for MSP online with Health Insurance

128
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:06,360
B.C.

129
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,740
It's free if your permit runs six

130
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:09,460
months or more,

131
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:11,480
and your card comes by mail.

132
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,880
Starting work:

133
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,980
give HR your SIN and bank details,

134
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,500
fill in the federal and B.C.

135
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,900
tax forms, and enrol in benefits fast.

136
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,860
Many plans give you thirty days,

137
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,940
and some match your retirement savings.

138
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:28,760
So what does a hundred and twenty

139
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:29,780
thousand pay?

140
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:33,360
Income tax takes about twenty five thousand.

141
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,140
Pension and employment insurance,

142
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,740
nearly six.

143
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,440
You keep about eighty nine thousand,

144
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:42,060
roughly seven thousand four hundred a month.

145
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,040
Here's a number that matters later.

146
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:47,860
Every dollar above about a hundred and

147
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,215
seventeen thousand is taxed at roughly thirty

148
00:04:50,235 --> 00:04:50,945
eight percent.

149
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,400
Housing:

150
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,220
never pay for a place you haven't

151
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,700
seen.

152
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:56,340
B.C.

153
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,420
deposits are capped at half a month's

154
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:00,240
rent, plus half for a pet.

155
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,060
No credit score?

156
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,500
Bring your offer letter and bank statements,

157
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,040
and get tenant insurance.

158
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,840
You can drive on your Indian licence

159
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,400
for ninety days.

160
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:13,500
India isn't on ICBC's exchange list,

161
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,740
so you'll take knowledge and road tests.

162
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:18,020
A letter proving two years of driving

163
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,560
skips the learner stages.

164
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,920
Part three:

165
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,120
your money in India.

166
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:26,320
Once you leave for a job abroad,

167
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:27,900
you're a non-resident Indian,

168
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,840
and your accounts must change.

169
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:33,500
Under FEMA, your savings accounts and fixed

170
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,860
deposits become NRO accounts.

171
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,380
Tell every bank.

172
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:39,860
Open an NRE account for money from

173
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:43,020
abroad, and merge three savings accounts into

174
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,440
one bank with good NRI service.

175
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,960
NRE holds money from abroad:

176
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,740
fully repatriable, with interest tax free in

177
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:52,200
India.

178
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,300
NRO holds Indian income.

179
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,300
Banks deduct about thirty percent on its

180
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,140
interest, and you can send out up

181
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,120
to a million US dollars a year.

182
00:06:02,090 --> 00:06:03,210
The catch:

183
00:06:03,230 --> 00:06:05,970
Canada taxes your worldwide income from the

184
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,090
day you arrive,

185
00:06:07,550 --> 00:06:09,630
so NRE interest goes on your Canadian

186
00:06:09,650 --> 00:06:10,590
return.

187
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:12,870
Indian tax you paid is credited,

188
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:14,090
so you aren't taxed twice.

189
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,080
Mutual funds and shares:

190
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:20,560
update your KYC to NRI and link

191
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:21,880
your NRO account.

192
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,720
Some fund houses refuse new money from

193
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:27,760
Canada residents, but existing units can stay.

194
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:30,760
Pause SIPs, and move shares to an

195
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,420
NRI demat account.

196
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,300
Your EPF can stay,

197
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,640
but a dormant account can stop earning

198
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,180
interest, and withdrawing before five years of

199
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,100
service is taxable.

200
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,940
NPS stays open:

201
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,500
update it to NRI,

202
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,900
and contribute from NRE or NRO.

203
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:49,440
Gold.

204
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:52,560
Jewellery you wear is personal,

205
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,320
and Canada doesn't ask you to report

206
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:55,020
it.

207
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,480
Keep it in a locker or with

208
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,020
family.

209
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,620
Gold biscuits are an investment,

210
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,340
and they count as foreign property.

211
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:05,120
India's tax year runs April to March.

212
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:07,483
Leave for a job after under one

213
00:07:07,503 --> 00:07:08,980
hundred and eighty two days in India

214
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,090
that year, and you're non-resident.

215
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:13,920
Leave later, and you're still resident that

216
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:16,360
year, so ask an adviser about the

217
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:16,820
treaty.

218
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,980
Part four:

219
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,980
tax and investing.

220
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,140
Remember those landing-day statements?

221
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,300
Here's why.

222
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:26,600
When you become a resident,

223
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:28,980
Canada treats you as if you sold

224
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,940
and bought back everything you own,

225
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:33,080
at its value that day.

226
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:35,660
Growth before you landed isn't taxed in

227
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,000
Canada.

228
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:38,540
Only the gain after landing is.

229
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,680
One more form,

230
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:42,320
T1135.

231
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:44,720
Skip it in year one.

232
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,480
After that, if your foreign investments cost

233
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,400
over a hundred thousand dollars,

234
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:50,580
report them every year.

235
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,380
Jewellery doesn't count.

236
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:56,380
Accounts, funds, shares and gold biscuits do.

237
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:58,720
In our example,

238
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:00,400
those add up to about forty eight

239
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:03,360
lakh rupees, around seventy thousand dollars.

240
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:04,480
Under the line,

241
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,300
for now.

242
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,800
Your first Canadian return is due April

243
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:10,740
thirtieth of the next year.

244
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:13,600
Report worldwide income from your arrival date

245
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,680
and claim credit for Indian tax.

246
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:18,800
In India, file by July thirty first

247
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:20,880
whenever you have Indian income.

248
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,660
The first time,

249
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,720
use an accountant who knows both countries.

250
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:27,320
Now, investing, in this order.

251
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:30,200
First, an emergency fund of three to

252
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:31,320
six months of costs,

253
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,840
in insured high interest savings.

254
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,840
Second, any employer match.

255
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,660
It's free money.

256
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,640
Third, your TFSA.

257
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,800
Room starts the year you arrive:

258
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:45,740
seven thousand dollars for twenty twenty six,

259
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,280
whichever month you land,

260
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,440
but nothing for earlier years.

261
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,720
Over contribute, and you pay one percent

262
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:52,420
a month.

263
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,970
Seven thousand a year for twenty years

264
00:08:55,990 --> 00:08:58,110
is a hundred and forty thousand put

265
00:08:58,130 --> 00:08:58,570
in.

266
00:08:59,030 --> 00:09:00,790
At six percent a year,

267
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:02,827
it grows to about two hundred and

268
00:09:02,847 --> 00:09:03,970
fifty seven thousand,

269
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:07,230
and none of that growth is taxed.

270
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,580
Fourth, if you might buy a home,

271
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,360
open an FHSA early:

272
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:13,820
eight thousand a year,

273
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,780
forty thousand in total.

274
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,580
It cuts your tax,

275
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,580
comes out tax free for a first

276
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,380
home, and its room only starts once

277
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,320
you open it.

278
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:26,420
Fifth, the RRSP.

279
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,040
Its room comes from last year's Canadian

280
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:31,125
income, so it starts in year two:

281
00:09:31,145 --> 00:09:34,273
eighteen percent, up to thirty three thousand

282
00:09:34,293 --> 00:09:36,300
eight hundred and ten dollars.

283
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:38,620
At a thirty eight percent top rate,

284
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:39,820
that's a real refund.

285
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:43,160
Inside them, most people do well with

286
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,300
one low cost,

287
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,720
all in one index ETF from a

288
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,920
discount brokerage, left alone.

289
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:52,500
